  "prompt_text": "The figure summarizes a proposed pathophysiologic cascade linking severe inflammation to impaired circulation and multi-organ injury. At the center is a systemic inflammatory response driven by immune activation, cytokine release, and neutrophil plugging. Pro-inflammatory mediators such as TNF, IL-1, and IL-6 connect this response to both brain and heart injury.\n\nReduced circulation appears to be a key downstream event. On the cardiac side, inflammatory signaling contributes to myocardial dysfunction, with notes suggesting myocardial stunning, troponin degradation, and disturbed calcium homeostasis. This weakened heart function then further lowers circulation. On the neurologic side, brain injury is associated with brain edema, decreased vasopressin, glutamate excitotoxicity, and a no-reflow phenomenon, again feeding into poor perfusion.\n\nThe diagram also emphasizes vascular and endocrine contributors. Adrenal insufficiency is shown as another factor worsening circulatory failure. In the vasculature, collapse of the microcirculation, capillary leak, increased adhesion molecules such as ICAM-1 and VCAM-1, and vasoplegia reinforce systemic inflammation and impaired flow. Disseminated intravascular coagulation is shown alongside this vascular failure, indicating clotting abnormalities as part of the same cycle. Overall, the image depicts a self-amplifying loop of inflammation, vascular dysfunction, organ injury, and shock-like hypoperfusion.",
